Product Philosophy

The dashboard is not:

an accounting dashboard,
a reporting tool,
a fiscal administration interface.

The dashboard is:

a guided workflow experience,
a reassurance layer,
a progress orchestration system.

The user must immediately feel:

"This is simple. The software is guiding me."

The experience should feel closer to:

Linear,
Stripe,
Notion AI,
than to accounting software.
Primary UX Objectives

The dashboard must:

reduce cognitive load,
reduce fiscal anxiety,
create clarity,
guide progression,
maintain user confidence.

The interface must communicate:

progress,
simplicity,
AI assistance,
calmness,
without exposing technical complexity.
Layout Architecture
Global Layout

Desktop layout structure:

Top navigation
Hero section
Workflow progress navigation
Main dashboard content
Documents analyzed section
Footer utility states

The page should use:

generous whitespace,
strong vertical rhythm,
clear section separation,
lightweight cards,
soft visual hierarchy.

Maximum content width:

1280px

Recommended padding:

desktop: 32px to 48px
tablet: 24px
mobile: 16px
Visual Hierarchy

Priority order:

Reassurance
Current progress
Recommended next action
Workflow navigation
Documents analyzed

Avoid visual competition.

The page must never feel:

dense,
dashboard-heavy,
enterprise-like,
data-driven.
Hero Section
Purpose

Immediately reassure the user.

The hero should communicate:

simplicity,
progress,
guidance,
automation.
Hero Content
Badge

Example:
"2025 LMNP Declaration"

Style:

subtle pill badge,
muted background,
small typography.
Headline

Recommended:

"Prepare your LMNP declaration simply."

Alternative:
"Your declaration is being prepared automatically."

Typography:

large,
premium,
calm,
highly readable.

Avoid:

aggressive marketing tone,
fintech style headlines.
Supporting Text

Example:

"Upload your documents. The AI prepares your declaration automatically. Simply review and validate before generation."

Maximum:

2 lines desktop,
3 lines mobile.
Primary CTA

Examples:

Continue my file
Resume declaration
Continue preparation

CTA must:

feel reassuring,
not sales-oriented,
not administrative.
Progress System
Overall Progress

Display:

single overall completion percentage.

Recommended:

progress ring,
or
lightweight horizontal progress bar.

Avoid:

KPI blocks,
charts,
analytics cards,
accounting summaries.
Progress Messaging

Examples:

"Your declaration is progressing well."
"Only a few steps remain."
"Documents are currently being analyzed."

Tone:

calm,
supportive,
lightweight.
Workflow Navigation
Structure

Horizontal workflow navigation.

Steps:

My Activity
Property
Loan
Amortization & Works
Income
Expenses
Validation
Navigation Behavior

Users can:

freely navigate,
skip steps,
return later.

No forced wizard behavior.

Step States

Possible states:

completed,
active,
incomplete,
missing information.

State visibility must remain:

subtle,
elegant,
non-stressful.

Avoid:

red warning patterns,
error-heavy interfaces.
Dashboard Main Content
Purpose

The main area should dynamically guide the next best action.

The dashboard must intelligently encourage:

progression,
completion,
validation,
without pressure.
Recommended Content Blocks

Possible blocks:

next recommended action,
incomplete information reminder,
pending validation,
uploaded documents summary,
declaration preparation status.

All blocks must remain:

lightweight,
visually calm,
easy to scan.
Documents Analyzed Section
Purpose

Create reassurance and trust.

This section proves:

uploaded files were received,
analysis is progressing,
the system is working.

The section should NOT become:

a document management system,
a backoffice,
a storage explorer.
Document Item Structure

Each item can contain:

document name,
detected category,
upload date,
analysis state.

Possible states:

analyzed,
processing,
incomplete,
missing pages,
unreadable.
Actions

Available actions:

view,
replace,
delete.

Actions should remain:

secondary,
discreet,
low visual emphasis.
Save System

Display subtle auto-save feedback.

Example:
"Automatically saved"

Display location:

top right,
or
below hero section.

Avoid:

technical sync indicators,
loading-heavy states.
AI Integration Philosophy

The AI must feel:

active,
invisible,
useful,
calm.

The UI should communicate:

automation,
intelligent assistance,
preparation progress.

Avoid:

OCR terminology,
AI jargon,
technical processing language,
extraction complexity.
Important States

The dashboard must support:

first login,
empty state,
partially completed file,
fully completed declaration,
processing documents,
missing documents,
validation ready,
blocked progression.

All states must remain:

premium,
calm,
supportive.

Never create stressful interfaces.

Component System

Recommended V2 components:

DashboardHero
DashboardProgress
WorkflowStepper
WorkflowStep
RecommendedActionCard
DocumentAnalysisList
DocumentAnalysisItem
AutoSaveIndicator
DashboardSection
